title: Editor Toolbar Buttons
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Legacy-Glyphs

''V1.0:'' Block and inline dropdowns now iterate marker tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker` and filter by the active vocabulary for the tiddler being edited. New vocabularies appear in the menu without a code change. See [[Vocabulary Engine]] and [[Migration to V1.0]].

''v1.0.0-beta-13:'' The block and inline dropdowns are native `<$select>` widgets. Selecting an option writes the chosen marker's `marker-icon` field into `$:/config/wikilabs/custom-markup/icons/glyphs/active` (block) or `.../icons/inline/active` (inline). The `add-glyph` and `remove-glyph` buttons enable only for markers with `max-level > 1` (e.g. `»` and `›`); `toggle-glyph` enables for any marker that is not `kind: inline-pair`.

!! Filter syntax note

The button-enable filters use `compare:integer:gt[1]` (TYPE first, then OPERATOR). The reverse order `compare:gt:integer[1]` returns no matches silently and falls to the `else` clause of the surrounding `then[X]else[Y]`, so a wrong-order filter looks like a wrong default rather than a syntax error.

